# Text is stored and checked out with LF endings, whatever the machine's
# core.autocrlf says. Git for Windows' installer sets core.autocrlf=true for
# the whole system, and a fresh clone there came out CRLF; the clone the owner
# works in had a repo-local core.autocrlf=false to keep it LF. Every file in
# the index was already LF, so this changed no stored file.
* text=auto eol=lf
